  "notes": "Xiaomi MiTV-MFTR0 (freeguy, MediaTek mt9653), China firmware OS2.0.23.0.RFTMATV\n(HyperOS TV 2), Android 11 (SDK 30). Second CN-firmware set from the same live\nsessions as MiTV-ASTR0 (see examples/xiaomi-mitv-astr0/); the same mechanisms carry\nover 1:1 from HyperOS TV 3 to HyperOS TV 2. Input routes, settings intents and app\ndiscovery for this model: docs/devices/xiaomi-mitv-mftr0-freeguy.txt; debloat and\nHome notes: docs/devices/xiaomi-mitv-mftr0-debloat-home.md.\nDisabled and lived with on 2026-10-22; everything verified per-package against\nthis firmware first (it ships no WPS, no com.mitv.overseaservice, and Android 11\nhas no AOSP adservices module packages).\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-mftr0/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-mftr0/debloat.txt com.mitv.tvhome\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nNotes from this firmware:\n- The standby/screensaver ads come from com.xiaomi.mitv.hyper.screensaver, same as\non OS3: a plain Activity with its own downloaded carousel; screensaver_enabled=0\ndoes not touch it. com.mitv.screensaver / com.xiaomi.mitv.advertise don't exist.\n- Keep com.xiaomi.mitv.smartpanel enabled (it is the Menu-button panel: source\nswitcher + wireless tiles). Do NOT add it here.\n- First ADB connect needs the on-TV \"允许USB调试\" RSA confirmation; ADB over TCP\nthen closes on every reboot (Settings -> 账号与安全 -> ADB 调试 to re-enable).\n- Check /data/app before classifying anything as a preload: an owner-installed\nMoonlight (com.limelight) sat in an early draft of this list until `pm path`\nshowed it was not a preload. It is intentionally absent here.\nXiaomi telemetry / ads / push",
